{
  "$comment": [
    "The CROSS-LANGUAGE conformance vector for the enrolment proof-of-possession (#1157), `POST /v1/tenants` `pop`.",
    "",
    "Contract: signed_payload = framed(`seam-enroll-pop-v1`) | framed(subject_aid) | framed(tenant) | framed(namespace) |",
    "framed(u64_LE(issued_at_ms)) | framed(nonce), with framed(x) = u32_little_endian(len_bytes(x)) | x.",
    "subject_aid, tenant, namespace and nonce are UTF-8 exactly as sent; issued_at_ms is Unix epoch MILLISECONDS as 8 raw",
    "little-endian bytes. subject_aid is `aid:pubkey:ed25519:` + unpadded base64url of the raw 32-byte Ed25519 public key",
    "of seed_hex; the client signs signed_payload with that key and sends",
    "pop = {issued_at_ms, nonce, signature: unpadded base64url of the 64-byte Ed25519 signature}.",
    "",
    "Ed25519 is deterministic, so `signature` is exact. Generated by an independent Python implementation",
    "(`cryptography`), not by the Rust one. NO bless mode: a mismatch is a contract break (a v2 domain tag), not a stale fixture."
  ],
